    "units": "Dimensions in mm (w = width along local x, d = depth along local y). Cost in SEK. Carbon in kg CO2e per item.",
    "purpose": "Dimensioned loose items for the apartment model. Every item carries the clearance it needs in front of it — the zone you must be able to stand, turn or transfer in for the item to actually be usable. That clearance is the difference between furniture that fits on a drawing and furniture that works in a room, and it is what makes a plan testable against a user group rather than just against an area figure.",
    "clearance_note": "clearance_front_mm is measured from the item's front face along its facing direction. clearance_side_mm, where present, is a transfer zone required on at least one side (WC, bed in care use). These zones may overlap each other — two chairs can share circulation — but may not be blocked by walls or by items that are not themselves clearance-sharing.",
    "provenance": "PLACEHOLDER — indicative Swedish 2026 figures for model development. Replace with supplier data via the intake schema."
  },

